{'symbol': 'MRNA', 'date': '2020-08-26 13:30:00', 'title': 'MODERNA SAYS AT 100 MCG DOSE, MRNA-1273 WAS GENERALLY SAFE AND WELL-TOLERATED IN ALL AGE COHORTS IN PHASE 1 STUDY', 'text': 'MODERNA - ANNOUNCES INTERIM RESULTS FROM OLDER ADULT COHORTS (AGES 56-70 AND AGES 71+) OF PHASE 1 STUDY OF MRNA VACCINE AGAINST COVID-19.MODERNA - AT 100 ΜCG DOSE, MRNA-1273 INDUCED CONSISTENTLY HIGH LEVELS OF NEUTRALIZING ANTIBODY TITERS IN ALL PARTICIPANTS IN 56-70 AND 71+ AGE COHORTS.MODERNA - AT THE 100 ΜCG DOSE, MRNA-1273 WAS GENERALLY SAFE AND WELL-TOLERATED IN ALL AGE COHORTS.MODERNA - ANALYSIS FOUND AT 100 MCG DOSE SELECTED FOR PHASE 3 STUDY, MRNA-1273 WAS COMPARABLY IMMUNOGENIC IN THOSE AGED 56-70 VERSUS YOUNGER ADULTS IN EARLY STAGE TRIAL.MODERNA - AT 100 ΜCG DOSE, ANTIBODY TITERS WERE 2- TO 3-FOLD ABOVE THOSE SEEN IN CONVALESCENT SERA.MODERNA - AT DAY 57, THE REPORTED GEOMETRIC MEAN TITER LEVELS WERE 267 FOR 18-55 YEAR OLD COHORT, 324 FOR THE OLDER ADULT COHORT.MODERNA - MRNA-1273 ELICITED TH1-BIASED CD4 T CELL RESPONSES IN THE 56-70 AND 71+ AGE COHORTS.MODERNA - AT DAY 57, GEOMETRIC MEAN TITER LEVELS WERE 242 FOR ELDERLY COHORT.MODERNA - NEUTRALIZING ANTIBODY TITERS AND T CELL RESPONSES IN 56-70 AND 71+ AGE COHORTS WERE CONSISTENT WITH THOSE REPORTED IN YOUNGER ADULTS.MODERNA - NO VACCINE-RELATED SERIOUS ADVERSE EVENTS HAVE BEEN REPORTED IN PHASE 1 STUDY.'}